Premium access

Payment process
User selects a subscription.

Backend creates a pending payment record.

Backend initializes a Paystack transaction.

User is redirected to Paystack checkout.

Paystack processes payment.

Backend receives the webhook.

Backend verifies the signature and transaction status.

Backend confirms the amount, currency and reference.

Subscription is activated.

User receives confirmation.

Security requirements:

Store Paystack secret keys in environment variables.

Never expose secret keys in frontend code.

Verify webhook signatures.

Use idempotency protection for payment processing.

Verify that the paid amount matches the intended amount.

Prevent duplicate subscription activation.

Handle failed, abandoned and refunded transactions.

Provide a way to reconcile payments and subscription expiry.

For recurring memberships, configure Paystack's supported recurring billing flow and handle subscription lifecycle events. Do not assume a successful one-time payment automatically creates recurring billing.

