Important architecture decision: Supabase Auth and Prisma
Use Supabase Auth as the authentication authority and PostgreSQL as the shared database.

Supabase Auth owns password credentials and authentication sessions.

The application maintains a public users profile record linked to the Supabase Auth UUID.

Prisma accesses application tables.

Supabase Row Level Security protects user-owned records.

Server-only service credentials are never exposed to browsers.

For Prisma connections, use the appropriate pooled database connection in serverless deployments and a direct connection for migrations.

This avoids creating two competing authentication systems.

