8.4 Additional database rules
The SQL above is the initial schema, not the complete authorization implementation.

Implement these rules before production:

Enable RLS on all tables exposed through Supabase.

Users can only access their own profiles, goals, sessions and notifications.

Published workouts and articles can be publicly read.

Draft content is visible only to authorized administrators.

Premium content requires server-side membership verification.

Admin role changes must only be performed by trusted server-side processes.

Users cannot write payment or subscription status directly.

Payment event IDs must be unique to prevent webhook duplication.

Use database transactions when recording payment and activating subscriptions.

Add foreign-key and status constraints through migrations.

Important: Do not rely on a client-side isPremium flag to unlock paid content. Check entitlement on the server for every protected resource.

